# Implementation Plan: DCRUST Campus Placement & Eligibility Portal Backend (V2)

Architect and implement a production-grade, secure, modular monolith backend for the **DCRUST Campus Placement & Eligibility Portal**, fulfilling all 79 V2 specification requirements with Node.js, Express.js, PostgreSQL, Prisma ORM, Zod, Socket.IO, and comprehensive testing.

---

## Architecture Overview

```mermaid
graph TD
    Client[React Frontend / HTTP Client] -->|HTTP Request| SecMid[Helmet & Rate Limiter & CORS & Cookie Parser]
    Client -->|WebSocket| SIO[Socket.IO Server]
    SecMid --> ReqLogger[Pino HTTP Logger]
    ReqLogger --> AuthMid[authenticate JWT in HttpOnly Cookie]
    AuthMid --> RbacMid[authorize Role: STUDENT / COMPANY / ADMIN]
    RbacMid --> ZodMid[Zod Validation Middleware]
    ZodMid --> Controllers[Modular Controllers]
    Controllers --> Services[Domain Services with Business Rules]
    Services --> Repos[Prisma Repositories / DAL]
    Repos --> DB[(PostgreSQL Database via Prisma)]
    Services --> NotifService[Notification & Audit Service]
    NotifService --> SIO
    NotifService --> DB
```

The system is structured as a **Modular Monolith** where business logic lives purely inside services, controllers remain thin HTTP orchestrators, and Prisma provides type-safe, indexed, relational access to PostgreSQL.

